    "long": "The work is deep, self directed and long horizon. Researchers frame questions, secure funding, design and carry out studies, publish in peer reviewed journals, and build a reputation in a specialist field, usually alongside teaching and supervising students. Progress is measured in publications, grants and contribution to knowledge, and independence of thought is central.\n\nTypical roles run from PhD researcher and postdoc to lecturer, senior lecturer, reader and professor, with parallel routes in research institutes and industry research labs. People work in universities, government and charitable research bodies, and the research arms of companies.\n\nCompetitive funding, pressure to publish and the growth of interdisciplinary and open research shape modern academic careers. It suits people with exceptional analytical curiosity, a drive toward true mastery of a subject, and the autonomy and independence to pursue questions over years."
