    "careerWorldId": "cw_care_support_work",
    "careerWorldTitle": "Care & Support Work",
    "short": "This is about supporting children and young people to grow, learn and stay safe, in youth work, residential care and family support. Its purpose is to give young people guidance, safety and someone in their corner.",
    "long": "This is caring, active work with children and teenagers, helping them develop, cope with challenges and make good choices.\\nTypical roles include youth support worker, residential childcare worker and family support worker. You would work in youth centres, care settings, schools and the community.\\nIt suits energetic, caring people who young people trust. You can start from Level 2 or 3 through college or a children and young people apprenticeship, with no degree needed."
